1
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:30,120
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

2
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:35,800
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

3
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,400
♪ I don't understand ♪

4
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,920
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

5
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:48,720
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

6
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:55,040
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

7
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:01,040
As for the contract, I'll take care of it
tomorrow and send it back to you.

8
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:04,319
You know what I want now, right?

9
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,880
I want my woman back.

10
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,160
Does Uncle know yet?

11
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,800
I've already informed the chairman's secretary

12
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:15,560
that Mr. Songsak finalized the deal
with Mr. Techin this morning.

13
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,160
I'll go to the office right away.

14
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,039
I want an explanation.

15
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:28,440
Someone reported to me
that we failed to secure the deal.

16
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:31,320
Songsak signed with a competitor this morning.

17
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:35,640
Didn't you promise you'd handle this properly?

18
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:39,000
I have no explanation. It was my mistake.

19
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,000
Is it because of that woman?

20
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:43,759
Phat told me everything.

21
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,880
You delivered her to the place.

22
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,920
Then what happened?

23
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,759
Trading a woman for a contract isn't work, Dad.

24
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:53,840
Why is it not, Peem?

25
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:57,440
It's business. We give them what they want
in exchange for what we want.

26
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,240
If it were an object, I wouldn't mind.

27
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,320
But it's a person. Don't you understand, Dad?

28
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:04,080
Peem, you've never acted like this before.

29
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:07,040
You didn't show up at the company. You didn't
answer your phone. You ran away from problems.

30
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:10,520
Do you know how much the company lost
because of what you did?

31
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:17,200
The Peem that I knew would never do this.

32
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,400
How did it go?

33
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,280
Let's go home.

34
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,000
Mr. Songsak signed with someone else?

35
00:02:58,760 --> 00:02:59,640
Yeah.

36
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,080
Then what are you going to do?

37
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,720
There's nothing I can do.

38
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,120
But no matter how many times I had to choose,

39
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,600
I'd still choose you.

40
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:21,360
I'm sorry for making you feel bad that night.

41
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,680
You see those stars?

42
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:53,320
You don't usually see them in the city
because there are so many lights.

43
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,480
In big cities like this,
there are so many successful people.

44
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:01,320
Just like those stars.

45
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,400
But there will be one star that stands out
more than the others.

46
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,880
No matter how many lights there are,

47
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,280
they can never overshadow it.

48
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,320
That's just like you.

49
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,800
No one can make you lose your light.

50
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,440
Are you trying to make me feel better?

51
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,800
I believe you can get through this.

52
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,600
As long as you don't give up,

53
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,120
you'll always find a way forward.

54
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:51,520
It's actually you.

55
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,760
You're the little star

56
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:56,680
that's shining the brightest in my life right now.

57
00:05:49,159 --> 00:05:52,080
(Techin - Please call me back. It's urgent.)

58
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,040
What is it? You said it's urgent.

59
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,000
I can't do that today.

60
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,920
But I will call you back when it's convenient.

61
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,280
Oh, you're up?

62
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,800
You were asleep, so I didn't want to wake you up.

63
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,440
I'm going to keep you company at work.

64
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,800
You told me that
just staying by your side is enough.

65
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,840
So I want to be by your side

66
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:36,880
when you have to face things like this.

67
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:45,080
Why do you have to say
such sweet things like that right now?

68
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,600
We won't make it to work.

69
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:52,920
I'm going to take a shower.

70
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,520
Are you inviting me?

71
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,280
I'm not.

72
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,360
I'm going to hurry and take a shower.

73
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,560
I don't want you to be late for work.

74
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,760
I'll get going.

75
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,000
Shall we go now?

76
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,760
Not yet.

77
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,920
Aren't you in a rush to leave for work?

78
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,920
I am.

79
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,880
If you're in a rush, I can do it myself.

80
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,240
No. No matter how much of a rush I'm in,
you always come first.

81
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,840
This doesn't concern you. Leave.

82
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,880
I need to talk with my daughter.

83
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,240
Yes.

84
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,920
Is this the woman?
The whore you picked up from a bar?

85
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,240
Couldn't you find anyone else?

86
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,960
I don't care that she's a woman.

87
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,880
But I do mind that you picked up a random nobody
and decided to wife her up.

88
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,760
Have you seen this news?

89
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:20,720
(Real estate empire heir,
Peem, Phakanee Traisuvetthiwat)

90
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,640
(Still happy and in love
after losing a major deal to a competitor)

91
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:28,240
You haven't even settled the contract issue
with the board yet.

92
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,360
And now you've caused a new problem.

93
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:33,920
Do you realize how much of a mess you caused?

94
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,720
Don't blame me, Dad.

95
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,840
I'm not blaming you. I'm blaming that whore.

96
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,440
Dad.

97
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:43,600
You shouldn't look down on her like that.
It's just her job.

98
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,880
What? Her job is just sitting and lying around.

99
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,600
That's what she's good at.

100
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,080
What's so special about it?

101
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:53,560
I just don't get why you made her
your personal assistant.

102
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,880
You just have her lounging around the house.

103
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:59,560
Are you being stupid
and getting fooled by a whore?

104
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,560
Dad!

105
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,120
Let me tell you something.

106
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,480
This kind of person always chooses money.

107
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,840
They'll go with whoever has it. Just like...

108
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,480
Why did you stop?

109
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:12,800
Did you just realize that
you're no different from me?

110
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,080
Yes, I was stupid.

111
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,960
I once fell for this kind of person.

112
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,560
That's why I'm warning you.

113
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,440
I don't want you to get hurt.

114
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:30,080
Because in the end, she'll choose money, not you.

115
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,120
I don't care.

116
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:33,600
You could love Mom. I can love Parn too.

117
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,800
I believe that she's not with me because of money.

118
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,200
Unlike what Mom did to you.

119
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,200
Hey.

120
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,680
You heard everything my dad and I talked about?

121
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,880
Yes.

122
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,920
My mom's a sex worker.

123
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,800
My relatives told me...

124
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,160
she intentionally got pregnant to trap my dad.

125
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:38,960
After she gave birth to me,

126
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,320
she demanded money from my dad
in exchange for me.

127
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,960
I have no memories of my mom,

128
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,320
only of what she did,

129
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,400
and what I heard from my relatives.

130
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:12,360
When I met you at Paradise that day,
I thought you're like my mom.

131
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,560
Trying to land a rich partner
to improve your life.

132
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:19,920
Trying to get close to me for money
and a comfortable life.

133
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,120
But after I got to know you
and spent some time with you,

134
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,000
I realized you'd never be like my mom.

135
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,280
Because money can't buy you.

136
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,080
Money can buy my time.

137
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,280
But it can't buy me.

138
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:05,080
I'm sorry for everything.

139
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:07,680
You don't need to apologize.

140
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,240
It's enough that you understand.

141
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:18,520
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

142
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:23,120
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

143
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,360
♪ I don't understand ♪

144
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:31,840
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

145
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:36,560
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

146
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:42,160
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

147
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:53,560
If the revenue keeps dropping,
I'm gonna need to shut the place down.

148
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:13,640
(Parn)

149
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:27,040
Mr. Te, why are you here? We're not open yet.

150
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,480
I haven't been able to get a hold of Parn lately.

151
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:32,880
I also...

152
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,360
haven't been in touch with her.

153
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:40,200
She said she'd call me back when it's convenient
but she hasn't called me yet.

154
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:44,120
Maybe she's decided to leave this line of work.

155
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:47,200
You mean Parn isn't coming back to work?

156
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,440
She won't accept me as a client anymore?

157
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,320
Isn't that a good thing, though?

158
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,640
A woman has managed to leave this place.

159
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,920
You're still thinking about it?

160
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,520
I tried to stop.

161
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:25,400
But I can't help it. I keep thinking about it.

162
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:33,160
You don't have to go
to the office tomorrow, right?

163
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,720
Don't overthink it.

164
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:49,200
I'm just having a fight with my dad.

165
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,560
I was just about to ask

166
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:00,800
if I can skip going to the office tomorrow.

167
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:06,480
I want to take a baking class.

168
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,400
Sure.

169
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,640
Where do you want to go?

170
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:14,560
I'll take care of the fees.

171
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,520
I'm not asking for your money.

172
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,680
But I want to pay for you.

173
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:35,440
I told you...

174
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,280
because I wanted to ask for your permission.

175
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,880
If doing something makes you happy,

176
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,120
you can go ahead and do it.

177
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,240
You sure you don't want a ride?

178
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,200
Yes, I'll go there myself.

179
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,640
Drive safely and get home early, okay?

180
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,360
Do your best, okay? See you later.

181
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:38,680
"Okay?"

182
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:56,920
Hello, Dad.

183
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,920
Have you talked to your dad?

184
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,440
No.

185
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:56,240
Parn, will you stay by my side
like this, always?

186
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,080
You called me Parn?

187
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,040
Your name is Parn.

188
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,880
But you don't normally refer to me by my name.

189
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:08,920
I do now.

190
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:36,000
Hello, Mr. Te.

191
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,720
Where are you, Parn? You told me
you'd call me back when it's convenient.

192
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,160
But you never called,
so I wanted to give it a try.

193
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,880
Is there anything you want?

194
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,600
I want to warn you about Mr. Songsak.

195
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:50,880
He won't give up easily.

196
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:54,840
He told me if he can't have you, no one can.

197
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,640
I think he's going to do something.

198
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:00,240
Okay, I'll be careful.

199
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,360
I don't think he'll do anything to you, Parn.

200
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:07,400
You mean he's going to hurt Ms. Peem?

201
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,120
Are you free today?

202
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,640
Can you come see me?

203
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:13,760
Okay, then let's meet at 3 p.m.

204
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:23,280
Mr. Songsak doesn't know how to lose.

205
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,480
You said he's going to hurt Ms. Peem.

206
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,640
Is it because of this?

207
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:31,360
Yes.

208
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,720
Ms. Peem got in his way.

209
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,520
And she humiliated him.

210
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:42,400
Could you help me find a way to meet him?

211
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,400
Sis.

212
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,640
Why are you back?

213
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:15,240
I joined a baking class today.

214
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,840
I baked some for you too.

215
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,680
Keep it.

216
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,160
It makes me fat.

217
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:34,320
Sis.

218
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:40,440
Are you mad at me for not telling you myself?

219
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:48,920
I'm sorry.

220
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:52,600
I just didn't have the courage.

221
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,040
I was afraid.

222
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,440
I didn't how to say it.

223
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,840
Just say you want to quit.

224
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
But you're like my older sister.

225
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,960
You've been taking care of me since I was a kid.

226
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:17,000
You gave me the chance
that got me to where I am today.

227
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,720
I don't want you to think that...

228
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,040
all ties are severed after I quit.

229
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:29,240
But I want them to be severed.

230
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:33,320
Sis.

231
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:45,160
I don't want you to come back
and work this job again.

232
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:49,800
I want you to go and have a good life.

233
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:52,280
Marry a rich person.

234
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,640
I will never cut ties with you.

235
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:04,000
Never.

236
00:24:22,080 --> 00:24:23,480
Does she take good care of you?

237
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:36,600
Does she show respect to my Angel?

238
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:49,080
If one day she hurts you,

239
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:51,720
you will always have me.

240
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,400
You know that, right?

241
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:34,200
It was on sale, so I bought it.

242
00:25:36,760 --> 00:25:39,640
That means you remember that I like it.

243
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:43,360
Yeah.

244
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,760
Why are you back early today?

245
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:54,080
There's nothing left to handle at the office.

246
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:58,080
That means you missed me.

247
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:02,440
Yeah.

248
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:07,160
And why are you back late today?

249
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:10,240
I stopped to buy some things.

250
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,760
Next time, wait for me and we'll go together.

251
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:17,080
You don't have a car, and things are heavy.

252
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,520
You should wait, so I can help you carry them.

253
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,040
Okay?

254
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:24,480
Okay.

255
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,680
What's wrong, Parn?

256
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:43,720
What is it?

257
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:52,680
I don't know how long this happiness will last.

258
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,080
It'll be long.

259
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,960
It could even last a lifetime.

260
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:11,640
I want to be with you, Peem.

261
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:17,040
I want to be with you all day and all night.

262
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:28,280
♪ We both said some awful words ♪

263
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:30,520
♪ And I know that we both got hurt ♪

264
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:31,880
♪ But I wanna be with you ♪

265
